(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #90. A buffer argument that is not a variable — a call's
 result, say — has no caller cell to write back to, so it is given one of its
 own. The callee is correct for the length of the call, and the growth dies
 with the temporary, because there is no caller variable for it to reach.
 What must NOT happen is the callee reading through an address that belongs
 to nothing.)

To 'a fresh buffer'.
    a buffer called made is "start".
    Return a buffer, made.

To 'pad out and measure' with a buffer called sink.
    a number called appended is 0.
    While appended is less than 600,
        append "0123456789" to sink,
        Set appended to appended add 1.
    Print "the callee sees: {sink's size}".

'pad out and measure' of 'a fresh buffer'.

a buffer called kept is 'a fresh buffer'.
'pad out and measure' of kept.
Print "the named one kept it: {kept's size}".
